L11.raw_latex:
\label{lem:zhanglinearinf}

Given a Hilbert space $\H$ and a mapping $\phi:\X\rightarrow \H$, let $\X \subseteq \{x\in\X : \|\phi(x)\|_{\H} \leq R_x\}$ and 
$\F = \{f \in \R^{\X} : \ f(x) = \inner{w}{\phi(x)}_{\H},\ \|w\|_{\H} \leq R_{w}\}$. 
Then, for any $\epsilon\in(0,R_x R_w)$,  
\begin{align*}
	\log \mathcal{N}_{\infty}(\epsilon, \F, n) &\leq 36  \frac{R_x^2 R_w^2}{\epsilon^2}  \log \left( 2\left\lceil \frac{4R_x R_w}{\epsilon} + 2\right\rceil n + 1\right) \\ 



	&\leq 36  \frac{R_x^2 R_w^2}{\epsilon^2}  \log \left(  \frac{15 R_x R_w n}{\epsilon} \right),  
\end{align*}
and for $\epsilon\geq  R_x R_w$, $\log \mathcal{N}_\infty(\epsilon, \F, n)=0$.

